The green light is `green:status` here too, for the reason 0002 gives: the
fallback in msm8916-ufi.dtsi names it `green:wlan`, which is what the GPIO sits
next to rather than what the light is for. cp2cl drives it with the same facts
it drives the NanoPi's by, and S56led beats it once the access point is on air.

The red and blue lights are already `red:power` and `blue:wan` and are left as
they are.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8916-thwc-ufi001c.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8916-thwc-ufi001c.dts
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 };
 
 &led_g {
+	function = LED_FUNCTION_STATUS;
 	gpios = <&tlmm 21 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 };
 
